parse.instruction:
Ignore Start with. Emit exactly one {"op":NAME,"arg":VALUE} per operation sentence, preserving sentence order and repetitions. Use these mappings:
reverse/reverse order -> reverse; ascending/smallest to largest -> sort_asc; descending/largest to smallest -> sort_desc;
remove/delete first k -> remove_first; keep/retain first k -> keep_first; remove all/delete every equal to x -> remove_all;
add/increase by k -> add; multiply/scale by factor k -> multiply;
keep even/remove odd -> keep_even; keep odd/remove even -> keep_odd;
rotate left/move first k to end -> rotate_left; swap/exchange first and last -> swap_ends;
append/place x after last -> append; remove duplicates/keep first occurrence -> unique.
For remove_first, keep_first, remove_all, add, multiply, rotate_left, append, arg is the stated integer. For all other operations arg is null. Never use a list value as an argument unless the instruction states it. Return {"ops":[...]} only, with no start field.
